{"version": 1, "sourceSha256": "f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d", "documents": [{"id": "offline-a86d67e84f765e0ffd6e", "filename": "READING 12.pdf", "sha256": "a86d67e84f765e0ffd6e56e5a767e6b84cab13b60274e2e8620486e57f215787", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/a86d67e84f765e0ffd6e56e5a767e6b84cab13b60274e2e8620486e57f215787.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/a86d67e84f765e0ffd6e56e5a767e6b84cab13b60274e2e8620486e57f215787.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}, {"id": "offline-f22eb48823921340245b", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 12.pdf", "sha256": "f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}], "units": [{"id": "a86d67e84f765e0f-p1", "label": "Part A · READING 12.pdf", "part": "A", "sourceSha256": "a86d67e84f765e0ffd6e56e5a767e6b84cab13b60274e2e8620486e57f215787", "pages": [1, 2, 3, 4], "questions": [{"number": 1, "prompt": "A. condition that occurs due to an increase in the number of white cells in the\nblood\nAnswer___________________.", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 185, "answer": {"text": "C", "source": {"id": "offline-f22eb48823921340245b", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 12.pdf", "sha256": "f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 2, "prompt": ".Often, it is not possible to deal with complications\nAnswer__________________.", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 304, "answer": {"text": "B", "source": {"id": "offline-f22eb48823921340245b", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 12.pdf", "sha256": "f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 3, "prompt": "Recorded to be more effective in dealing with the disease conditions\nAnswer_______________.", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 389, "answer": {"text": "D", "source": {"id": "offline-f22eb48823921340245b", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 12.pdf", "sha256": "f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 4, "prompt": "homicide of virtually all other parts of the cell by the enzymes\nAnswer_________________.", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 487, "answer": {"text": "A", "source": {"id": "offline-f22eb48823921340245b", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 12.pdf", "sha256": "f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 5, "prompt": "Almost fortnightly for effective management\nAnswer__________________.", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 583, "answer": {"text": "D", "source": {"id": "offline-f22eb48823921340245b", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 12.pdf", "sha256": "f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 6, "prompt": ".Not-so-common when compared to other medical conditions\nAnswer____________________.", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 658, "answer": {"text": "A", "source": {"id": "offline-f22eb48823921340245b", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 12.pdf", "sha256": "f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 7, "prompt": ".Weakening appearance\nAnswer___________________.", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 748, "answer": {"text": "B", "source": {"id": "offline-f22eb48823921340245b", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 12.pdf", "sha256": "f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 8, "prompt": ".What is the common reason for Gaucher Disease?\nAnswer_________________.", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 954, "answer": {"text": "lysosomal system defects", "source": {"id": "offline-f22eb48823921340245b", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 12.pdf", "sha256": "f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 9, "prompt": "Is it still clear how disease appears in its various forms or not?\nAnswer____________________.", "sourcePage": 3, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1032, "answer": {"text": "Not clear yet", "source": {"id": "offline-f22eb48823921340245b", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 12.pdf", "sha256": "f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 10, "prompt": "ERTs available include?\nAnswer____________________.", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 0, "answer": {"text": "imiglucerase", "source": {"id": "offline-f22eb48823921340245b", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 12.pdf", "sha256": "f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 11, "prompt": ".What can lead to anaphylaxis?\nAnswer____________________", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 60, "answer": {"text": "Antibody production", "source": {"id": "offline-f22eb48823921340245b", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 12.pdf", "sha256": "f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 12, "prompt": "What is regarded as medically clean or without infection?\nAnswer___________________.", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 125, "answer": {"text": "aseptic", "source": {"id": "offline-f22eb48823921340245b", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 12.pdf", "sha256": "f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 13, "prompt": ".What happens when Gaucher cell penetrate more deeply?\nAnswer_________________.", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 218, "answer": {"text": "thrombosis, infarction", "source": {"id": "offline-f22eb48823921340245b", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 12.pdf", "sha256": "f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 15, "prompt": "The__________ have the capacity to exterminate various other cell structures.", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 600, "answer": {"text": "lysosomal enzymes", "source": {"id": "offline-f22eb48823921340245b", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 12.pdf", "sha256": "f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 16, "prompt": "With the appearance of red marrow, the___________ and__________ often get\naffected more badly and may lead to infarction.", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 683, "answer": {"text": "vascularity", "source": {"id": "offline-f22eb48823921340245b", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 12.pdf", "sha256": "f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 17, "prompt": ".The two of the common conditions that can occur due to Gaucher may\ninclude _________ and _____________.", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 810, "answer": {"text": "anemia", "source": {"id": "offline-f22eb48823921340245b", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 12.pdf", "sha256": "f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 18, "prompt": ".It is requisite to monitor_______________ during the first year.", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 919, "answer": {"text": "Immunoglobulin G antibodies", "source": {"id": "offline-f22eb48823921340245b", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 12.pdf", "sha256": "f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 19, "prompt": "Enzyme replacement therapy is known to be more effective in curtailing down\nthe____________ and improving osteopenia.", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 989, "answer": {"text": "incidence of hepatosplenomega", "source": {"id": "offline-f22eb48823921340245b", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 12.pdf", "sha256": "f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 20, "prompt": "Studies reveal that there are various other __________ which can make the\nconditions worse.", "sourcePage": 4, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1112, "answer": {"text": "bone injury mechanism", "source": {"id": "offline-f22eb48823921340245b", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 12.pdf", "sha256": "f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}], "skills": ["reading"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-f22eb48823921340245b", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 12.pdf", "sha256": "f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}], "passages": []}, {"id": "a86d67e84f765e0f-p5", "label": "Part B · PART B", "part": "B", "sourceSha256": "a86d67e84f765e0ffd6e56e5a767e6b84cab13b60274e2e8620486e57f215787", "pages": [5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11], "questions": [{"number": 1, "prompt": "------ is an epidemic of infectious disease that has spread across a large region\nDisease Transmission\nBioterrorism\nPandemics\nEmerging infectious diseases\nEmerging infectious diseases impact healthcare providers in the United States and\nglobally. Nurses play a vital role in protecting the health of patients, visitors, and\nfellow staff members during routine practice and biological disasters, such as\nbioterrorism, pandemics, or outbreaks of emerging infectious diseases. One vital\nnursing practice is proper infection prevention procedures. Failure to practice\ncorrectly and consistently can result in occupational exposures or disease\ntransmission. Infection prevention education based on existing infection\nprevention competencies is critical to ensure adequate knowledge and safe practice\nboth every day and in times of limited resources.", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 222, "answer": {"text": "Pandemics", "source": {"id": "offline-f22eb48823921340245b", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 12.pdf", "sha256": "f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 2, "prompt": "What is the risk of passing CMV to the baby during pregnancy?\nA Baby gets infected quickly\nB There is more risk if the infection is primary\nC Low risk in the first two trimester compared to the third trimester.\nTransmission\nIn general, 1 of every 150 to 200 babies in the USA is born with congenital CMV.\nThis makes CMV the most frequent congenital viral infection. Though this seems\nlike a large percentage of births, only 1 in 5 of these infants born with congenital\nCMV will experience any adverse symptoms or long-term issues.\nThe virus has the potential to travel through the mother’s blood and pass through\nthe placenta, infecting the developing baby.\nIf the pregnant lady contracts the virus (primary infection) during pregnancy: It is\nmore likely to pass on CMV to the baby if it is primary infection during the\npregnancy. If the mother has a primary CMV infection during pregnancy, there is\napproximately a 40% chance of passing the virus to the baby.\nThe risk of transmission from mother to baby is highest if she gets a primary CMV\ninfection in the third trimester (40-70%) and is lowest if the primary infection\nbegins in the first or second trimesters (30-40%).", "sourcePage": 6, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 0, "answer": {"text": "C Low risk in the first two trimester compared to the third trimester.", "source": {"id": "offline-f22eb48823921340245b", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 12.pdf", "sha256": "f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 4, "prompt": "What is wrong?\nA Not effective with respect to QRS complex\nB Mental disease occurs more often\nC Medication shall be used again and again\nAtropine IV/IM (Rx) - Warnings\nCaution in hepatic/renal impairment, BPH, CHF\nNot for effective treatment of type II second or third-degree AV block with or\nwithout a new wide QRS complex\nUse caution in autonomic neuropathy, myocardial ischemia, heart failure, paralytic\nileus, hepatic impairment, hiatal hernia associated with reflux esophagitis,\nhyperthyroidism, myasthenia gravis, and renal impairment\nHeat prostration can occur in a high environmental temperature\nPsychosis reported in sensitive individuals and with excessive doses\nWhen a recurrent use of atropine is essential in patients with coronary artery\ndisease, total dose should be restricted to 2 to 3 mg (maximum 0.03 to 0.04 mg/kg)\nto avoid detrimental effects of atropine-induced tachycardia on myocardial oxygen\ndemand", "sourcePage": 8, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 0, "answer": {"text": "Is: B Mental disease occurs more often", "source": {"id": "offline-f22eb48823921340245b", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 12.pdf", "sha256": "f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 6, "prompt": "According to the table given, which is correct?\nA The mean age in diabetics is significantly greater than that in non-diabetics\nB more than 60% are male\nC The difference of BMI in diabetics and non-diabetics is very less\nSummary statistics of subjects classified in diabetic and non-diabetic subgroups based on\nFBS >126 mg/dl.\nUnivariate P-\nNon-diabetics     Diabetics\nvalue\nCategorical Variable\n(%) Frequency\nFrequency\n(%)\nSex                       Female         296 (56.3)        51 (64.6)           0.171\nmale           229 (43.7)        28 (35.4)\nMarriage status           Married        456 (86.9)        77 (97.47)          Ù .006\nsingle         69 (13.1)         2 (2.53)\nEducation                 Illiterate     35 (6.7)          11 (13.92)          Ù .072", "sourcePage": 10, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 0, "answer": {"text": "A The mean age in diabetics is significantly greater than that in non-diabetics", "source": {"id": "offline-f22eb48823921340245b", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 12.pdf", "sha256": "f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}], "skills": ["reading"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-f22eb48823921340245b", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 12.pdf", "sha256": "f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}], "passages": []}, {"id": "a86d67e84f765e0f-p12", "label": "Part C · READING 12.pdf", "part": "C", "sourceSha256": "a86d67e84f765e0ffd6e56e5a767e6b84cab13b60274e2e8620486e57f215787", "pages": [12, 13, 14, 15, 16, 17, 18, 19, 20], "questions": [{"number": 10, "prompt": "What do we learn about medication in the fourth paragraph?\nA .Glucocorticoids are very effective\nB .Recommends only the use of non-steroidal anti-inflammatories\nC .Medications can lead to dysglycemia\nD . it brings in more benefit to make use of steroids when the conditions are to\nbe dealt with immediately", "sourcePage": 15, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 517, "answer": {"text": "D It brings in more benefit to make use of steroids when the conditions are to", "source": {"id": "offline-f22eb48823921340245b", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 12.pdf", "sha256": "f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 15, "prompt": "According to paragraph 1, XDI scanner;\nA. is more powerful than any other scanners\nB. can provide accurate data\nC. is developed merely to deal more effectively with explosive material\nD. doesn`t just transmit x-ray data", "sourcePage": 19, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 24, "answer": {"text": "A is more powerful than any other scanners", "source": {"id": "offline-f22eb48823921340245b", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 12.pdf", "sha256": "f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 22, "prompt": "In the last paragraph, ` in vivo ` may mean\nA. To apply externally\nB. Happening or existing inside a living body\nC. To be more challenging\nD. To overcome complexities", "sourcePage": 20, "choices": ["A", "B", "C", "D"], "kind": "question", "offset": 305, "answer": {"text": "B Happening or existing inside a living body", "source": {"id": "offline-f22eb48823921340245b", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 12.pdf", "sha256": "f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}], "skills": ["reading"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-f22eb48823921340245b", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 12.pdf", "sha256": "f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/f22eb48823921340245b3eaa66ac5748115fcf4149c6dd533db50a175debde1d.json", "f